{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBranchingRule","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBranchingRule","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBranchingBijection"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.numStandardYoungTableaux_branching","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.numStandardYoungTableaux_branching","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranchingRule.lean#L83-L91","doc":"**The structural GNW branching count.** For a non-empty Young diagram,\n`numStandardYoungTableaux μ = ∑_{removable corners c} numStandardYoungTableaux (μ ∖ c)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.branchInv_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.branchInv_injective","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranchingRule.lean#L48-L81","doc":"`branchInv` is injective: the inserted corner is recovered as the unique max-value cell, then the\ndeletion roundtrip pins the tableau. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.branchInv_surjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.branchInv_surjective","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranchingRule.lean#L41-L46","doc":"`branchInv` is surjective: every `T` is the re-insertion at its max corner of the deletion of that\ncorner. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.branchInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.branchInv","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranchingRule.lean#L36-L39","doc":"The inverse branching map on the corner-indexed disjoint union: re-insert `|μ|` at corner `c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.fintypeCorners","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.fintypeCorners","kind":"instance","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranchingRule.lean#L28-L34","doc":"The removable corners of `μ` form a finite type (they sit inside the finite cell set). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.instDecidableIsCornerCell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.instDecidableIsCornerCell","kind":"instance","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranchingRule.lean#L25-L26","signatureChunk":0}]}